<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

`<<~ pranala from="lar:///a.b.c/x" -> to="lar:///a.b.c/y">>` names an edge. It takes `from`, `to`, `slot`, `family`, `role`, `body` and an optional `template`; the block form wraps a body between the open and `<<~/pranala>>`. Absent `family`, the edge reads `relation`.

''A fragment resolves against the carrier.'' A `from` or `to` that opens with `#` gains the current tiddler as its prefix, so `#/head` addresses this carrier's own child rather than a bare fragment.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/parse-exception>>

!! The Permanent Parse Exception

Pranala keeps a permanent JS exception in `lar-sigil.ts`. Its arrow syntax — FROM `->` TO plus keyword attributes — stands structurally apart from the `<<~ WORD ARGS>>` shape every other sigil wears, so `findNextMatch` matches it directly BEFORE compound dispatch fires. `PRANALA_OPEN_RE` and `matchPranalaOpenAt` in `lar-sigil-shared.ts` carry that match.

The sibling exception, `pranala-header`, spends `?` as a self-reference token for this carrier: `<<~ ? -> uri>>`. It parses in the same pre-dispatch pass and renders through its own cascade.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/template-cascade>>

!! The Template Cascade

An explicit `template` parameter wins; absent one, the widget takes the first tiddler tagged `lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/pranala-template`, and falls back to `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/templates/pranala/html`.

The shipped template renders a `<span class="lar-pranala">` carrying `data-from` and `data-to`, adding `data-family` and `data-role` only where those read non-blank, linking both ends, and folding a non-blank `body` into a `<details>` note.

`pranala-header` renders `<span class="lar-pranala-header">` with `data-canonical-uri` and a single link, through `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/templates/pranala-header/html`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/source>>

